meta {
  name: NewProductVersion
  type: graphql
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/graphql-api
  body: graphql
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  x-xtm-hub-token: {{xtm-hub-token}}
}

body:graphql {
  mutation NewProductVersion($product: PlatformIdentifier!, $version: String!) {
    newProductVersion(product: $product, version: $version) {
      success
    }
  }
}

body:graphql:vars {
  {
    "product": "opencti",
    "version": "6.260409.0"
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Ensure xtm-hub-token is defined in environment (requires GENERATE_MANIFEST capability)
  
  Fill variables:
  product: PlatformIdentifier enum value (e.g. opencti, openaev)
  version: product version, e.g. 6.4.0, or an LTS version, e.g. 7.260309.0-lts.8
  
  Behaviour:
  - Any invalid version is rejected (INVALID_PLATFORM_VERSION), LTS or not. The LTS suffix must be lowercase (-lts.N).
  - A non-LTS version requests the connector manifest generation and registers the version.
  - An LTS version (-lts.N suffix) skips the manifest generation and the registration.
  - For opencti, every valid version also creates one GITHUB_RELEASE news feed item, once per version (a later call
    with the same version does nothing, even once the item is deleted), provisioned to the active OpenCTI platforms on the
    same release track (LTS or not) whose version passes the gate of that track. This step runs in the background
    and never fails the mutation.
}
